WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.720
Brooks, here's the walkthrough of the TDHCA

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.760
follow-up I've put together for the team.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.800
I'll show you the timing, who's responsible

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.240
for the calls, what the emails offer,

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.960
and what happens when someone asks for

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.660
help. First, one distinction: the eight online

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:17.413
tools and their submission handling are live.

00:00:17.413 --> 00:00:19.780
This thirty-six-month email journey is still a

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.787
draft, with nobody enrolled.

00:00:21.787 --> 00:00:23.120
So what we're looking at here is

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.680
the configured follow-up, not a campaign that's

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:31.080
already sending. The process starts with the

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.040
TDHCA leads coming into the CRM.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.440
The importer matches existing contacts where it

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:39.120
can, keeps the source history, and registers

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.800
the contact in the TDHCA group.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.400
Being in that group isn't the same

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.507
as being enrolled in this flow.

00:00:45.507 --> 00:00:47.100
The daily handoff is part of the

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.480
setup; I'm keeping verification of the current

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.600
import schedule separate from turning on the

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.480
nurture. We don't need to create a

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.400
second contact or a deal just to

00:00:55.400 --> 00:01:00.960
begin following up. Scott owns the call

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.400
follow-up in this journey.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.280
There are five call tasks: day zero,

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.120
day two, day five, day nine and

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.160
day thirteen after enrollment.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:11.920
Day zero means the day the person

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:14.240
enters the journey. These are tasks for

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.827
Scott to work, not automatic phone calls.

00:01:16.827 --> 00:01:18.720
Keep that separate from the workbook submissions

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:20.187
we'll look at in a minute.

00:01:20.187 --> 00:01:22.320
When someone sends a completed workbook, that

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:23.947
task goes to Brooks.

00:01:23.947 --> 00:01:25.760
The call plan and the workbook handoff

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:31.180
have different owners. For the first twelve

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.320
weeks, the email schedule has three slots

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:36.440
each week: education on day zero, another

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.920
educational email on day two, and a

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.760
resource offer on day four.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:43.080
Those days are relative to enrollment, not

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.827
a fixed Monday, Wednesday and Friday schedule.

00:01:45.827 --> 00:01:48.160
From week thirteen onward, it's education on

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:49.880
day zero and an offer on day

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:52.040
four. The configured time is nine in

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:54.200
the morning, Chicago time, with the lead's

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.387
send window also respected.

00:01:56.387 --> 00:01:58.760
The journey runs for thirty-six calendar months,

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:00.900
rather than a fixed number of days.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.400
Here's a sample educational message, and here's

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.200
an offer asking the buyer to reply

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:10.320
with a keyword. The emails come from

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:13.040
Brooks's team domain. Replies go into the

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.120
CRM and are configured to forward to

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.147
the BK team mailbox.

00:02:17.147 --> 00:02:20.560
The keyword rules are Payment, Cash, Credit,

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:24.587
Ready, Compare, Shop, Offer and Plan.

00:02:24.587 --> 00:02:26.880
A matching reply sends the appropriate resource

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.700
link. After the provider accepts that resource

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:31.600
email, the rule alerts the team and

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.960
creates a same-business-day follow-up task for Scott.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:37.380
A normal reply doesn't stop the nurture.

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:42.460
Now let's open the resource library.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.840
Payment helps somebody write down a comfortable

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:47.480
payment range, what a quote includes, and

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.920
what would be left after their other

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:52.080
costs. Cash separates the money available from

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:53.520
the money they want to keep and

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.660
the costs they still need estimated.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.600
Credit gives them a place to describe

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.520
a concern or ask about a change

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:02.160
they're considering. Ready helps them track what

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.520
the lender requested, what they have, and

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.020
what they need help getting.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.520
These collect their answers and questions; they

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.140
don't make lending decisions.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.520
Compare puts two loan estimates and the

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:17.540
questions about their differences together.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.200
Shop compares two homes, including costs, needs

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.280
and concerns that might not be obvious

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.520
from the price. Offer keeps the dates

00:03:25.520 --> 00:03:27.680
someone has actually been given, where each

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.720
date came from, and the next task

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:31.060
and person handling it.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.040
Plan brings together when they'd like to

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:35.280
move, what they already know and the

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.740
next question to ask.

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.147
Nothing here picks a winning loan, invents

00:03:39.147 --> 00:03:41.280
a deadline or turns a blank amount

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:46.360
into zero. Let me show the handoff

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.460
using an example, without sending it.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.840
I'll enter a question, then choose Send

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:52.140
to Brooks for review.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:54.120
The person can check the answers before

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.680
the final send. Sending requires a name

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.920
and email; phone is optional.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.480
Once submitted, the answers become a CRM

00:04:01.480 --> 00:04:03.480
note, a task for Brooks and a

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.160
queued team notification. They aren't enrolled in

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:07.960
the email journey by doing this.

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:09.560
They can also print or save their

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:12.240
answers without entering their contact details.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:14.300
The header keeps Book a call and

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.100
Apply now available, with Brooks's calendar and

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:23.380
application link. An opt-out stops the nurture.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.520
Closing or funding a loan doesn't remove

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:26.960
someone from this follow-up.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:29.760
Ordinary replies, bookings and a human taking

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.880
over don't automatically stop it either.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.600
The configured advertising audience sync follows the

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:37.280
same retention intent: keep closed and funded

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:40.200
contacts, remove explicit opt-outs.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.080
These are separate systems, though.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:43.880
Being in the audience doesn't mean someone

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:46.000
is enrolled in this email journey, and

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.520
audience syncing doesn't prove that retargeting ads

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:53.720
are currently running. Everything we've just looked

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:55.640
at stays editable in the native Flow

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:57.480
Builder and the linked tools.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.680
Before the email journey goes live, we

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:02.280
still need the remaining consent, message clearance

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:05.240
and send checks, followed by deliberate activation

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.840
and enrollment. Scott has the scheduled calls

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.560
and keyword follow-up tasks.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:12.200
Brooks gets the submitted-workbook tasks, and the

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.220
team gets the notifications.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.120
That's the handoff I want everyone to

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:19.260
understand: useful help for the buyer, their

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:21.560
actual question in the CRM, and a

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:24.530
clear person responsible for the next conversation.
